/**
@page exa_time_dg_cantilever Energy-corrected time DG cantilever forward analysis

The forward input exercises report.pdf's DG(1), alpha=4 scheme.
The input selects linear plane-strain elasticity or finite-deformation StVK through
gDGNonlinear. The domain is the cantilever [0,3]x[0,h], clamped at x=0.
A horizontal GEN level set y-h=0 cuts the upper surface out of a [0,3]x[0,0.8]
background mesh with 12x4 elements, Q2 B-splines and conformal XTK integration.
Phase 0 is the only active material. mu=3, lambda=5 correspond to E=7.875,
nu=0.3125. Reference density is one. The clamp uses symmetric Nitsche and
cut-cell stabilization uses ghost-normal-field terms; both receive the same
reduced weak/collocation time treatment as bulk forces.

@section exa_time_dg_forward Forward manufactured solution

Time_DG_Cantilever_Forward applies manufactured body force and reference
tractions for u=(0,-a*x^2*t), with a=0.025, h=0.43, six slabs and final time
T=0.3. Initial displacement is zero and initial velocity is (0,-a*x^2).
The motion has det(F)=1. It is represented exactly by the Q2 spatial and
linear temporal bases; its temporal acceleration is zero. The separate pulse
sensitivity example exercises nonzero inertia over multiple slabs.

Writing k=-2*a*x*t and c=lambda/2+mu, the StVK first Piola stress is
 P=[[c*k^2,mu*k],[mu*k+c*k^3,c*k^2]].
The linear stress has off-diagonal entries mu*k and zero diagonal entries.
The body load is -Div(P), and every unclamped boundary receives P*N.
Callbacks use reference coordinates and sample endpoint loads consistently.

check_results reads VIS Exodus output and checks dimensions, stored local
node/element counts, coordinate bounds, final time, and every local beam node's
analytical displacement. The global references are
 integral(u_y)=-9*a*T*h and volume=3*h.
These analytical references apply to both constitutive models and both process
counts. Verified local mesh references are 200 nodes/72 elements on one rank
and 104 nodes/36 elements on each of two ranks. Polynomial fields and exact
integrals supply the physical references. Unused void vertices retained by
VIS are excluded from displacement checks. Nodal DG output samples the outgoing
trace, and final IQIs use spatial quadrature at the last slab endpoint.
The tip corner (3,0) must occur in at least one rank's local output. All MPI
collectives are outside rank-specific branches, and readers are closed before
collective result checking. gPrintReferenceValues prints local mesh statistics.


The separate @ref exa_time_dg_cantilever_sensitivity example under
projects/EXA/optimization/Time_DG_Cantilever_Sensitivity verifies the adjoints.

The input is a self-contained .cpp file with direct MORIS includes. The shared
EXA main initializes MORIS/Catch, and each CTest case has its own working
directory. Driver globals select linear or nonlinear elasticity; standalone
input builds supply their own defaults. No environment-variable configuration
or PETSC_OPTIONS is required.

@section exa_time_dg_commands Build and execution
@verbatim
cmake --build build_dbg --target Main_Time_DG_Cantilever --parallel 4
ctest --test-dir build_dbg -R '^Time_DG_Cantilever-Forward' --output-on-failure
@endverbatim
*/
